/* Modern theme for the system menu -- #panel now consumes base.rcss's .modern-frame/
   .modern-frame-crimson (applied in sys_menu.rml, this file's own themed fork) instead of its own
   bespoke flat fill, same family as login/msg_win/my_quest_info's frame. No title-glow banner
   here -- this dialog has no title text for one to sit behind (just 4 stacked buttons), so it
   gets the frame material without the glow; that's a real, narrower difference from the other
   dialogs, not a missed spot. Buttons rely entirely on base.rcss's shared .btn.

   #panel is not C++-positioned/sized -- centered via base.rcss's .center-both
   utility class (applied in sys_menu.rml), fixed dp size matching CWinEx's own real geometry
   exactly (213 = the panel art's sprite width; 187/155 = TOP.height(64) + BOTTOM.height(43) +
   LEFT.texHeight(8) * 10-or-6 lines, SysMenuWin.cpp's SetLine() math -- 10 lines in the character
   scene, 6 in the login scene, toggled here via .compact rather than pushed from C++). Every
   button below is a fixed dp offset from the panel's own edges -- SetPosition()'s old per-button
   math (SMW_BTN_GAP=4, base offsets 33/height-52) is now baked into these numbers directly, no
   scene-awareness needed since exit-game/select-server anchor from the top and option/close
   anchor from the bottom (bottom-anchoring absorbs the .compact height difference for free).

   #btn_option/#btn_close's `bottom` values are the old C++'s "distance from panel bottom to the
   button's TOP" (86/52) minus the button's own 30dp height, not those numbers directly -- CSS
   `bottom` measures to the button's BOTTOM edge, not its top. Using 86/52 as-is would put every
   bottom-anchored button 30dp higher than intended, overlapping #btn_select_server above it. */
#panel {
	width: 213dp;
	height: 187dp;
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
	font-size: 12dp;
	color: token(text-body);
	border-radius: 10dp;
}
#panel.compact {
	height: 155dp;
}

#btn_exit_game    { left: 52dp; top: 33dp; }
#btn_select_server{ left: 52dp; top: 67dp; }
#btn_option       { left: 52dp; bottom: 56dp; }
#btn_close        { left: 52dp; bottom: 22dp; }
